<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak c.bank reserves down to $3.605 bln - Sept 4.</title>
<headline>Slovak c.bank reserves down to $3.605 bln - Sept 4.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) on Monday said its hard currency reserves fell to $3.605 billion as of September 4, from $3.714 billion on August 27.</p>
<p> HARD CURRENCY RESERVES     Sept 4   Aug 27   Sept '95</p>
<p>  NBS reserves ($bln)	 3.605    3.714    2.825</p>
<p>  Commercial banks	    1.254    1.234    1.581</p>
<p>  Entire banking sector     4.859    4.948    4.406</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
</text>
